    "target_geometry": "Exact current selected canonical feature geometry read from two pinned part blobs; only its envelope was transformed to native-grid x/y, with x=(lon+180)/360*262166 and y=(0.5-ln((1+sin(lat))/(1-sin(lat)))/(4*pi))*262166, matching src/pixel-grid.js.",
    "run_intersection": "Union source_feature_indices from each complete source-candidate-block run intersecting the target geometry native-grid envelope. Envelope is conservative; a candidate run indicates native-raster source support somewhere in the bbox, not polygon intersection with target.",
    "limits": [
      "Screen uses source-candidate runs and indexes for blocks 36/37; families that geometrically overlap target but produce no native raster candidate-cell center in bbox may be omitted.",
      "This does not prove polygon-level intersection or disjointness, legal territorial status, ancestry, or a complete source_evidence negative-family list.",
      "SWZ ADM1 rows are broad tier context, not direct owner vectors or negative families.",
      "Stock sourceTerritorialExclusions requires full original source bodies for selected negative families."
    ],
    "candidate_family_interpretation": "Five non-SWZ families have candidate raster feature spans inside at least one full canonical target-geometry native-grid bbox: MOZ ADM1/ADM2 and ZAF ADM1/ADM2/ADM3. These are bounded candidates to acquire and compare under stock sourceEvidence. They are not proven target polygon intersections or legal territorial exclusions. The 4 SWZ ADM1 features are explicit parent-tier context only; SWZ ADM2 is the positive family.",
    "candidate_family_observations": [
      "No MOZ ADM1 candidate occurs inside target-specific point candidate rows; MOZ families are flagged by raster candidate spans intersecting the full Mhlume, Lomahasha and Tikhuba geometry envelopes.",
      "ZAF ADM1/ADM2/ADM3 families are flagged by raster candidate spans within the Ngwempisi and Zombodze geometry envelopes.",
      "The family-level screen is conservative within native source-candidate coverage of the computed target bboxes, but the bbox screen can include features outside the exact target polygon and can omit non-rasterized tiny features."
    ]
  },
